Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: Movable, collapsible tools with an actual README demonstration.
Dependencies: 66_SETTINGS_BACKDROP_DISMISS.todo,68_COMPLETE_README_REFRESH.todo.

Purpose
-------
Let the user reposition or hide the bottom action strip without losing tools.

Tasks
-----
[x] Add a dedicated mouse/touch grip and accessible collapse/expand control.
[x] Clamp to player bounds after moving, expanding, resizing and fullscreen.
[x] Support arrow-key movement, Shift for larger steps and Home to reset.
[x] Preserve actions and skip-link access; Escape cancels a drag before menus.
[x] Exercise real touch cancellation, desktop movement and small-phone fit.
[x] Record and review actual movement/collapse GIF; add it to the README.
[ ] Publish and monitor this deployment under the user's renewed authorization.

Acceptance criteria
-------------------
No accidental game action from dragging. Hidden actions leave the focus order.
The collapsed grip/expander remain reachable. Moving/resize never strands the
dock offscreen. Existing handlers, 44px targets and power-switch clearance stay.
Default position/collapse are page-session state, not new stored preferences.
README demonstration is actual footage, not a mockup or supplied-ROM test.

Completion evidence
-------------------
Desktop movement/collapse/expand/cancel/Home and real CDP touch movement/cancel
pass locally. Responsive existing test retains all controls and power clearance;
390px uses two rows, 320px uses three with the two new controls.
First Escape attempt exposed the existing capture-phase menu handler; resolve
cancellation in that existing handler, not a competing target-only listener.
Initial CLI backslash test-file expression matched no tests; use dock.spec.mjs.
Skip-link test awaits drawer-close focus before activating the link; no assumed
Shift-Tab order. Final drag/reset case repeats twice. Syntax/build/12 units pass.
